Article 3 (Procedures, Methods, and Standards for Management Evaluations, etc.)
(1) Pursuant to Article 34 (1) and (2) of the Act, the Minister of Health and Welfare shall, within six months after the end of each fiscal year, conduct an evaluation of the management performance of City/Do Institutes for the preceding year (hereinafter referred to as a "management evaluation") and an evaluation of the job performance of their heads (hereinafter referred to as a "performance evaluation").
(2) The Minister of Health and Welfare shall prepare guidelines for management evaluations and performance evaluations (hereinafter collectively referred to as "evaluations, etc.") and notify the heads of City/Do Institutes thereof by January 31 each year.
(3) For the evaluations, etc. under paragraph (1), the head of a City/Do Institute shall submit the following matters to the Minister of Health and Welfare within three months after the end of each fiscal year:
1. The extent to which the terms of the performance agreement under Article 21 (1) of the Act have been fulfilled;
2. The current status and results of implementation of major projects;
3. The current status of organizational, personnel, and financial management;
4. The financial statements for the preceding year;
5. Management performance over the most recent three years.
(4) The head of a City/Do Institute shall reflect the results of evaluations, etc. in formulating the business plan for the following year.
